{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-162704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nrepresents the linear transformation that acts on a vector in ${R}^{2}$ as follows (in the order given):\n\n- It rotates the vector  $\\pi $ radians counterclockwise about the origin, then\n\n- stretches the result by a scale factor of $3$ parallel to the $x$-axis, and finally\n\n- reflects the result about the $x$-axis.\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-162704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $P$ be the matrix that represents the rotation, $Q$ be the matrix that represents the stretching, and $R$ be the matrix that represents the reflection. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nHence, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $RQP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RQP & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n$a+b=(-3)+1=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-162704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c66080d2d9bd906356b57790ee24eb6002a60cbb7d637a0ccec9042390b3f18"} {"question" "q-162704" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-162704" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-162704" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-277771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Construct the matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T$ that acts on a vector in ${R}^{2}$ as follows (in the order given):\n\n- It rotates the vector by $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians **clockwise** about the origin, then\n\n- stretches the result by a scale factor of $5$ parallel to the $x$-axis, and finally\n\n- shears the result with a shear factor of $3$ parallel to the $x$-axis.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $0$ |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-277771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $P$ be the matrix that represents the rotation, $Q$ be the matrix that represents the stretching, and $R$ be the matrix that represents the shearing. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\,\n$$\n\nHence, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $RQP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =RQP \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-277771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c66080d2d9bd906356b57790ee24eb6002a60cbb7d637a0ccec9042390b3f18"} {"question" "q-277771" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-277771" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-277771" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-277771" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-277771" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-277771" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-279666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Construct the matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T$ that acts on a vector in ${R}^{2}$ as follows (in the order given):\n\n- it shears the vector by a shear factor of $\\frac{1}{3}$ parallel to the $x$-axis, and then\n\n- scales the result by a scale factor of $3$ with center of enlargement at the origin.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-279666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $P$ be the matrix that represents the shear, and let $Q$ be the matrix that represents the scaling. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ Q & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $QP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =QP \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-279666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c66080d2d9bd906356b57790ee24eb6002a60cbb7d637a0ccec9042390b3f18"} {"question" "q-279666" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-279666" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/