my/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-279667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $P$ be the matrix that represents the shear, and let $Q$ be the matrix that represents the scaling. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ Q & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $QP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =QP \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-279667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c66080d2d9bd906356b57790ee24eb6002a60cbb7d637a0ccec9042390b3f18"} {"question" "q-279667" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-279667" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557ab