stion-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-279670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $P$ be the matrix that represents the rotation, $Q$ be the matrix that represents the stretching, and $R$ be the matrix that represents the shearing. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\,\n$$\n\nHence, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $RQP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =RQP \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-279670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c66080d2d9bd906356b57790ee24eb6002a60cbb7d637a0ccec9042390b3f18"} {"question" "q-279670" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069720/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17920487ab2cc8f95ef31cd390963c557abeb7c60399d3997c9fe5ee395dac7"} {"question" "q-279670" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.ty